# =========================
# Node.js (Tools/)
# =========================

**/node_modules/
# Scratch tarballs of the admin dashboard (Tools/_dash*.tgz) — build artifacts of the
# Next.js/open-next bundle, regenerable, never authored. 2026-08-18.
Tools/_dash*.tgz

# =========================
# Huge assets (over GitHub's 100MB limit or re-downloadable)
# =========================

# Third-party asset packs (re-downloadable from Asset Store)
Assets/Packs/

# Generated course scenes (regenerated from terrain data)
# Use /* (not trailing /) so negation rules for Experimental/ are still evaluated
Assets/Golf/Courses/*/Generated/*
!Assets/Golf/Courses/*/Generated/Experimental/
!Assets/Golf/Courses/*/Generated/Experimental/**

# Original imported scene lightmaps & reflection probes
Assets/Scenes/Original/

# Large binary source files
*.unitypackage
*.psd
*.tga
*.TGA
*.exr
*.EXR

# Bot demo-video transient artifacts (BotFrameRecorder → build_bot_video.py)
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/botframe_*.png
tasks/loop_v2_smoke_bot/*/video/

# Session-local lock/sentinel files dropped into _capture/ by smoke runners.
# These should never have been tracked (rolled back in dae6f451, 2026-05-26).
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/*.flag
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/*.flag.pre

# =========================
# Daily Report tool (Docs/Scripts/daily_report.py)
# =========================
# Secrets (.env) and the per-machine venv must never be committed.
Docs/Scripts/.env
Docs/Scripts/.venv/
Docs/Scripts/daily_report.log
Docs/Scripts/.last_sent
Docs/Scripts/.today_note
# Python bytecode regenerated whenever the report runs.
Docs/Scripts/__pycache__/
# Media drop folder: contents are transient (auto-deleted after send).
# Keep only the scaffold.
Docs/Reports/Media/*
!Docs/Reports/Media/README.md
!Docs/Reports/Media/.gitkeep

# =========================
# Python bytecode (GLOBAL) — 2026-05-31
# Previously only Docs/Scripts/__pycache__/ was ignored, so .claude/hooks/
# __pycache__/*.pyc got committed. Ignore bytecode everywhere.
# =========================
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# =========================
# Diagnostic scratch captures — transient working output. 2026-05-31
# Tracked .jpg/.txt/.log evidence already in _capture/ is unaffected; durable
# review evidence now lives in per-task Docs/Specs/.../screenshots/ folders.
# =========================
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/*.png
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/**/*.png
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/orbit_frames*/

# =========================
# GreenSlope authoring-tool captures — local-only, regenerable via
# Tools/GreenSlope/scripts/capture-all-holes.mjs. Cesar: ignore (2026-06-01).
# =========================
Tools/GreenSlope/screenshots/

# =========================
# green_orbit_videos: 544MB of green orbit clips (16 holes × normal+slope-grid).
# Kept LOCAL per Cesar (2026-06-01) — reviewed in-folder, regenerable via the
# green-orbit recorder + GreenSlopeGridOrbit helper. Docs/screenshots ARE tracked.
# =========================
Docs/Specs/Completed/green_orbit_videos/videos/
Docs/Specs/Active/green_orbit_videos/videos/

# Spec verification videos — local-only, regenerable from orbit tooling (large; per green_orbit_videos precedent 2026-06-02)
Docs/Specs/**/videos/

# Physics verification videos — same rule as Docs/Specs/**/videos/ above (2026-08-06,
# cup_capture_and_lipout). Physics specs live under Docs/Physics/ rather than Docs/Specs/,
# so the glob above misses them; the three cup clips alone are 69 MB and are regenerable
# from GOLFIN > Smoke > Loop v2 > Cup — …. Docs reference the paths; the bytes stay on disk.
Docs/Physics/videos/

# =========================
# Transient run-output / scratch dirs (Cesar 2026-06-11). These are regenerable
# capture/bot outputs and Unity auto-recovery scratch that the team has purged
# repeatedly (1db82d7f, a7c10956). Already-tracked files in them stay tracked;
# this only stops NEW untracked noise from dirtying the working tree.
# =========================
Assets/_Recovery/
Docs/Diagnostics/_capture/
tasks/loop_v2_smoke_bot/
# Orphaned intermediate review frames from a shipped task (canonical stills already committed)
Docs/Specs/Completed/1v1_match_flow/screenshots/

# =========================
# Order-350 (sound_effects) unused audio — keep on disk, out of git (Cesar 2026-06-16).
# Verified against the shipped SfxLibrary.asset (24 clip GUIDs) + every tracked
# scene/prefab/asset: NONE of the files below are referenced by the game. The clips
# the build actually uses are already committed — the golf Hit/Land/Swing sounds as
# .ogg, plus card_draw_1/2.wav, card_fan.wav and Victory/Clapping_01/02.wav. The
# remainder is an unused commercial pack and uncompressed .wav source twins of the
# shipping .ogg. SfxLibrary loads clips only via direct SO refs (no Resources.Load),
# so a clean clone still builds with full sound. .gitignore never untracks, so the
# already-committed clips above are unaffected.
# =========================
# Entire 400 Sounds Pack library is unused except the 3 already-committed Card and Board clips.
Assets/Sounds/400 Sounds Pack/
# Uncompressed .wav source twins of the shipping .ogg golf sounds.
Assets/Sounds/Hit/*.wav
Assets/Sounds/Hit/*.wav.meta
Assets/Sounds/Land/*.wav
Assets/Sounds/Land/*.wav.meta
Assets/Sounds/Swing/*.wav
Assets/Sounds/Swing/*.wav.meta
# Unused .ogg variants not referenced by SfxLibrary (Landing_Grass / _02).
Assets/Sounds/Land/Golfin_SFX - Landing_Grass.ogg
Assets/Sounds/Land/Golfin_SFX - Landing_Grass.ogg.meta
Assets/Sounds/Land/Golfin_SFX - Landing_Grass_02.ogg
Assets/Sounds/Land/Golfin_SFX - Landing_Grass_02.ogg.meta

# Completed-task review screenshots (kept on disk, not tracked) — mirrors 1v1_match_flow
Docs/Specs/Completed/map_view_aiming/screenshots/
Docs/Specs/Completed/sound_effects/screenshots/
Assets/Scenes/Original~/

# general_shop_ui review screenshots — kept on disk, not tracked (mirrors 1v1_match_flow)
Docs/Specs/Completed/general_shop_ui/screenshots/

# =========================
# Spec review screenshots — GENERALIZED (2026-07-28, Order 1240 close-out).
# Per-task screenshot folders had been added one-by-one after the fact (see the
# 1v1_match_flow / map_view_aiming / sound_effects / general_shop_ui lines above),
# and the rule was missed every time until someone noticed. ob_boundary_presentation
# reached 169 files / 557 MB untracked before it was caught at close-out review —
# one `git add .` from being permanently in history.
#
# Mirrors the `Docs/Specs/**/videos/` rule above: review evidence is local-only and
# regenerable via the capture bots. Reports reference the paths; the bytes stay on disk.
# .gitignore never untracks, so every screenshot already committed stays committed.
# =========================
Docs/Specs/**/screenshots/

# =========================
# build_version_stamp — the anti-staleness build stamp is GENERATED at build time
# (and on every editor play-mode enter) by BuildStampGenerator, then read back at
# runtime from Resources. It changes on every build by design, so it is never
# tracked — mirrors the ProjectSettings restore that keeps buildNumber out of git.
# =========================
Assets/Resources/Data/build_stamp.txt
Assets/Resources/Data/build_stamp.txt.meta

# =========================
# upload_guard_automation — run log of Tools/mark-uploaded.sh, appended by the Xcode
# Archive post-action on every archive. It is the ONLY diagnostic for a guard that did
# not advance (the script always exits 0 so Xcode never surfaces a failure), which makes
# it a per-machine debugging trail, not shared history. The guard file it writes
# (Docs/Versioning/last_uploaded_build.txt) stays TRACKED — that one is shared truth.
# =========================
Docs/Versioning/.mark-uploaded.log

# =========================
# iOS export residue — Unity re-drops these into Assets/ on every iOS player
# build (BuildPipeline.BuildPlayer / Build & Run). They are generated build
# artifacts, never authored, and were hand-deleted twice before being ignored
# (see Docs/Reports/2026-08-04_ios_simulator_build_blocker.md §9, §12).
# =========================
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRunInfo.json
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRunInfo.json.meta
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRunSettings.json
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRunSettings.json.meta
Assets/packages-merged-link/
Assets/packages-merged-link.meta

# =========================
# Auth secrets (Sign in with Apple .p8 etc.) - NEVER commit
# =========================
Secrets/

# =========================
# fastlane_testflight_pipeline — `fastlane ios testflight_build` run artifacts.
# fastlane/Fastfile, Appfile and .env.example ARE tracked; everything below is
# per-run or per-machine. The App Store Connect .p8 must live OUTSIDE the repo
# entirely (~/.appstoreconnect/) — the *.p8 rule is a backstop, not the plan.
# Builds/ipa/ is already covered by [Bb]uilds/ above; listed explicitly so the
# .ipa is obviously accounted for.
# =========================
fastlane/.env
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/README.md
fastlane/test_output/
Builds/ipa/
*.p8
